---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '@/components/ui/Container.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button.astro';
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildOrganizationSchema } from '@/lib/seo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Infinity Stone Solutions collects, uses, and protects information on this website. Includes analytics, form submissions, and security compliance disclosures."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
  noindex={true}
  structuredData={[
    buildOrganizationSchema(),
    buildBreadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <PageHero
    title="Website Privacy Policy & Security Compliance Statement"
    description="How Infinity Stone Solutions collects, uses, and protects information on this website. Last updated March 15, 2026."
  />

  <section class="section-space">
    <Container className="max-w-4xl">
      <div class="mb-6 flex justify-end">
        <Button href="/privacy/print" variant="secondary" analyticsEvent="privacy_pdf_download" analyticsLabel="privacy-print">
          Download PDF
        </Button>
      </div>

      <div class="panel rich-copy p-8 md:p-10">

        <h2>Privacy Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          For Infinity Stone Solutions Inc. (ISS), data protection is not merely a regulatory checkbox; it is a
          fundamental strategic requirement for a partner within the U.S. Defense Industrial Base (DIB). Our
          organizational philosophy is anchored by our core values: <strong>Innovation, Integrity, and Mission
          Success</strong>. We believe that "Integrity" in how we handle stakeholder information is the prerequisite
          for the "Mission Success" we deliver to the federal government. This policy serves as a transparent roadmap
          of our commitment to data stewardship, ensuring that our security posture matches the high-consequence nature
          of the services we provide.
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose my-6 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-[var(--color-border)]">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] text-sm">
            <div class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Legal Entity</div>
            <div class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] px-5 py-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">Infinity Stone Solutions Inc. (ISS)</div>
            <div class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Service Pillars</div>
            <div class="px-5 py-3 text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">Cloud & IT Modernization, AI & Analytics, GIS & Geospatial, Cybersecurity, and Program Management</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>Strategic Alignment: Federal Transparency</h2>
        <p>
          As a trusted provider for agencies including the DoD, DHS, and DOI, ISS is held to a higher standard of data
          stewardship than traditional commercial entities. Because we operate at the intersection of national security
          and technological innovation, our privacy protocols are designed to protect the integrity of the information
          ecosystem surrounding our federal engagements. This ensures that every stakeholder — from a citizen visitor
          to a government contracting officer — can interact with our digital presence with absolute confidence.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Collection: Voluntary vs. Automatic</h2>
        <p>
          ISS categorizes information collection into distinct streams to maintain full transparency.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Voluntary Information</h3>
        <p>Collected when you interact with ISS through the contact inquiry form or direct email.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Engagement data:</strong> Name, professional email address, company or organization, phone number (optional), area of interest (optional), and message content.</li>
          <li><strong>Processing:</strong> Submitted inquiries are processed through a third-party transactional email service and delivered to the ISS business inbox. This information is used solely to respond to your request.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Automatic Technical Data — Hosting</h3>
        <p>
          This website is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare's</strong> infrastructure. Like most hosting platforms, Cloudflare
          automatically logs technical indicators during user sessions — including IP addresses, browser type, and request
          metadata — for security, performance, and reliability purposes.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Automatic Technical Data — Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          This website uses <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand how visitors engage with the site at a high
          level. Google Analytics collects standard website usage data — such as page views, session duration, browser
          type, and approximate geographic location — along with high-level interaction events like CTA clicks and form
          completions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google Analytics uses cookies to distinguish unique visitors and maintain session state. These are first-party
          cookies set in your browser and can be cleared at any time. Analytics data is processed by Google as a service
          provider and is used by ISS for marketing measurement only. You may opt out using the
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-primary)]">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Automatic Technical Data — Spam Prevention</h3>
        <p>
          The contact form uses an automated verification service to confirm that submissions are from human users.
          This process may collect limited browser signals and is used solely for spam prevention purposes.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Utilization and Ethical Constraints</h2>
        <p>
          ISS operates under a strict <strong>"No Sale of Data" pledge</strong>. We do not sell, rent, or trade
          personal information to third parties. Stakeholder data is never treated as a commodity. The utilization of
          collected information is strictly limited to three primary objectives:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Business Inquiry Response:</strong> Facilitating professional outreach and the delivery of mission-critical services.</li>
          <li><strong>Website Security and Integrity:</strong> Monitoring the digital environment to prevent unauthorized access, system degradation, or cyber threats.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal and Regulatory Compliance:</strong> Ensuring all data handling aligns with federal mandates and existing legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>CMMC Alignment and Technical Security Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          As a contributor to the U.S. Defense Industrial Base, ISS has architected its security posture to align with
          the Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification (CMMC) and NIST standards. We employ a "defense-in-depth"
          strategy to protect sensitive information from evolving global threats.
        </p>
        <p>Key technical controls include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Internal Enclave Strategy:</strong> ISS maintains a strict physical and logical separation between its public-facing website and its internal contract enclave. All contract-related data and Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) are processed in a secure environment isolated from the commercial website infrastructure.</li>
          <li><strong>Identity and Access Management:</strong> We implement Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) and stringent "least privilege" access controls to ensure only authorized personnel interact with sensitive systems.</li>
          <li><strong>Advanced Encryption:</strong> Industry-standard encryption is utilized for all data both at rest and in transit.</li>
          <li><strong>Vetted Cloud Architecture:</strong> ISS exclusively utilizes third-party cloud providers that have been vetted against rigorous federal security benchmarks.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Resilience: Minimizing the Attack Surface</h3>
        <p>
          By maintaining a logical isolation between the commercial website and the CMMC-regulated contract enclave,
          ISS effectively minimizes the attack surface. This architecture ensures that user data from the website never
          enters the secure enclave where government-sensitive information is stored, providing a hardened barrier that
          protects both our corporate integrity and our clients' mission-critical data.
        </p>

        <h2>Individual Data Rights and External Governance</h2>
        <p>
          ISS recognizes the evolving global landscape of data rights. We view these rights not just as a legal
          requirement, but as a commitment to accountability that mirrors the rigorous auditing requirements of CMMC.
          Regardless of location, we facilitate the ability for individuals to exercise the rights of
          <strong>Access</strong>, <strong>Correction</strong>, and <strong>Deletion</strong> of personal data held
          by ISS. To exercise these rights, contact us at the address below.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">External Links Notice</h3>
        <p>
          This website may contain links to external platforms, including government agency sites and third-party
          services. ISS does not exercise control over, and is not responsible for, the privacy practices or technical
          security of these external sites.
        </p>

        <h2>Policy Governance and Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy and Security Compliance Statement is a living security artifact. It is reviewed
          periodically and updated to reflect the latest in federal regulatory requirements and cybersecurity best
          practices. By ensuring all stakeholders — from individual citizens to CMMC assessors — clearly understand
          the ISS security posture, we provide the reliable foundation necessary for continued Innovation, Integrity,
          and Mission Success in the federal sector.
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface)] px-6 py-5 text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
          <p><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Last Updated:</strong> March 15, 2026</p>
          <p class="mt-1"><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Authority:</strong> ISS Security Office (Lead ISSO)</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            For inquiries regarding this policy or our data protection protocols, contact ISS security leadership at
            <a href="mailto:info@infinitystonesolutions.com" class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-primary)]">info@infinitystonesolutions.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
